<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Oil prices have fallen for a sixth session=
, dropping further below $100 a barrel on reports of increased supply from =
the Middle East and amid hopes of progress in talks between the US and Iran=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Asian stock markets have risen for a sixth=
 session, riding high on the artificial intelligence wave.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Brent crude is down about $1 at $98.32 a b=
arrel, after closing below $100 a barrel yesterday for the first time in mo=
re than two weeks. If the downward move is sustained over the day, the six-=
day declines would be the longest losing run for oil since August 2025, acc=
ording to Bloomberg.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Reuters reported, citing sources, that Sau=
di Arabia has restarted operations at its east-west pipeline and may have a=
lready resumed exports from the Red Sea port of Yanbu.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Donald Trump talked of progress in talks w=
ith Iran in New York but also threatened to =E2=80=9Cannihilate=E2=80=9D th=
e country if there was no deal.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Iranian president, Masoud Pezeshkian, =
addresses the UN general assembly later today and, according to reports, ma=
y meet the US president.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Chinese president, Xi Jinping, arrives=
 in Washington later today for talks with Trump, with speculation a trade t=
ruce between the US and China will be extended, and hopes that they can agr=
ee a cooperation deal over AI. Trump commented on AI in his speech at the U=
N yesterday, calling it =E2=80=9Csuper intelligence=E2=80=9D and <a href=3D=
"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyT=
NtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECyyyKiIcsbT_mvO_CmKOtXLza_Fs1LYxzDFtByENu551JfyTMNPRiD_C=
